window.docContents[157].resolve({"/#Graph-Theory-in-Lean":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"","header":"Graph Theory in Lean","id":"/#Graph-Theory-in-Lean"},"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity":{"contents":"* isoSigmaConnectedComponents: the isomorphism between G and the sigma graph of\n  its connected components.* EdgesInOneComponent: every edge of G lies in a single connected component (any\n  two non-isolated vertices are reachable from each other).* locallyFiniteDeleteEdges: the graph G.deleteEdges s obtained by deleting edges\n  from a locally finite graph is locally finite.* IsVertexConnected: predicate for a graph being k-vertex-connected.* Finset.fiberProj: the vertices z of G whose copy (z, b) in fibre b of\n  G □ K₂ lies in a given vertex set.* edgeConnectivity / λ(G): the edge connectivity\n  λ(G) : ℕ∞, the supremum of the k for which G is\n  k-edge-connected.* vertexConnectivity / κ(G): the vertex connectivity\n  κ(G) : ℕ∞, the supremum of the k for which G is\n  k-vertex-connected.* walkComponent: the set of vertices of a finite set W reachable from v₂ by a\n  walk lying inside W.* IsCutVertex: x is a cut vertex of G (some two vertices other than x are\n  joined by a walk, but every walk between them passes through x).* CycleEquivalent: two edges are cycle-equivalent if they are equal or lie on a\n  common cycle.* BlockEquivalent: the equivalence relation on edges generated by\n  CycleEquivalent.* blockOf: the subgraph spanned by all edges block-equivalent to a given edge.* blockSetoid: the setoid instance on G.edgeSet given by block-equivalence.* Block: a block of G, i.e. a block-equivalence class of edges.* blockMk: the block containing a given edge.* Block.toGraph: the subgraph underlying a block.* blockOfHom: an injective homomorphism maps the block of e into the block of\n  e.map f.* Block.map: the image of a block under an injective homomorphism f, the block\n  containing the images of its edges.* Block.mapHom: an injective homomorphism f maps each block B into the block\n  B.map f hf.* SplitsAt: G is the union of two proper subgraphs whose supports meet in at most\n  a given vertex.\n\nFrom the exercises:\n\n* botComponentEquiv: equivalence between the connected components of the empty\n  graph and its vertex type.* Hom.sigmaDesc: the universal property of the disjoint union: a family of\n  homomorphisms G i →g H gives a homomorphism Σg G →g H.* bowtie: two triangles sharing a vertex, a graph with κ(G) < λ(G).\n\n","context":"Graph Theory in Lean\u0009Appendix\u0009Definitions","header":"14.2.9. Chapter 10: Connectivity","id":"/Appendix/#section-chapter-10-connectivity"}});